# Rows to merge into docs/TECH-DEBT.md

Source: Phase 1 for `play/src/front/Chat/Components/Room/RoomTimeline.svelte` (2026-11-12). Baseline `HEAD` = `87b3c6e03`, `RoomTimeline.svelte` sha256 `e1743a01…cf57fae69`. Evidence: `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase1-roomtimeline/README.md`. Line numbers are `HEAD`'s.

## Debt Ledger rows

| Item | Location | Type | Risk | Effort | Priority | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| RT-01: the timeline hands `$readReceipts` to every message row, so each receipts update hands new props to every loaded row, although `Message.svelte` reads receipts only for the user's own messages (`hasReadReceipt` requires `isMyMessage`, `Message.svelte:120-131`). In a Matrix room every member's receipt triggers an update (`MatrixChatRoom.ts:328-343`, at most one per 250 ms burst), so the work per receipt grows with the loaded rows, and the receipts grow with the active members. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:1021` | performance (the eight-user freeze) | medium. Counted in the fakes: one receipts update re-hands props to 20 of 20 rows. The main-thread cost in a browser is not measured. | XS (pass the receipts to the user's own rows only) | P2 | fixed by `fix-RT-01.patch` (one line); pinned in `characterization-tests.patch`, test flipped to 2 of 20 rows |
| RT-02: the room is marked read on every new last message while the tab is visible, also while the user reads history. The jump button then says "2 new messages" for two messages that the read receipt already reports as read, and the other members see the user as a reader. `a93d1eeab` chose "read while the room is open" and skipped hidden tabs because "a hidden tab has not seen anything"; a user scrolled up has not seen them either. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:488-509` | quirk (two features that disagree: `a93d1eeab` and `f435d69a9`) | low to medium (read receipts that claim more than the user saw) | S (also require `autoScroll`, so the receipt follows the user back to the bottom) | P3 | pinned ("marks the room read … also while the user reads history …"); product decision, no fix in this phase |
| RT-03: a focus request pending when the room opens is focused twice: the `$roomTimelineFocusStore` effect runs when `initialMessagesLoaded` turns true, and `focusPendingTimelineRequestOrScrollToBottom` runs right after it in `initMessages().finally(...)`. Both pass `hasPendingTimelineFocusRequest` before either sets `lastTimelineFocusSequence`, so `scrollIntoView` runs twice and the highlight class is removed and added twice. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:233-237`, `:368-370`, `:457-463`, `:741-777` | bug (two owners for one action) | low (a second smooth scroll to the same target, measured in the fakes; a request that needs `ensureTimelineEventVisible` asks the room twice, inferred from the code) | XS | P3 | fixed by `fix-RT-03.patch` (`focusTimelineEvent` focuses one request at a time: a second call for the request in flight returns at once, and the open still skips its bottom scroll); pinned, test flipped from two calls to one |
| RT-04: a focus request whose event the room cannot load (`ensureTimelineEventVisible` returns `false`) never advances `lastTimelineFocusSequence`, so it stays pending. The open then neither focuses nor scrolls to the bottom or to the "New messages" line, and the room stays where the first pages left it. Every later retry tries the request again. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:457-463`, `:762-764` | bug (minor) | low (a stale link to a deleted message) | S (consume the request when it cannot be shown, and fall through to the normal open) | P3 | open; not pinned (inferred from the code) |
| RT-05: `dayLabel` reads `get(LL)` and `new Date()` inside `renderItems`, so "Today" and "Yesterday" are computed when the timeline changes, not when the day or the locale does. A room left open past midnight keeps "Today" on yesterday's messages until the next message. Each separator also builds a new `Intl.DateTimeFormat` on every timeline change. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:257-272`, `:281-299` | quirk | low | S (a day store that ticks at midnight, and one formatter per locale) | P3 | open; not pinned |
| RT-06: `myChatID` is read once, when the component is created. Own-message detection (the scroll on send, the new-messages count, the "New messages" line) keeps the id of that moment if the chat identity changes while the timeline stays mounted. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:83` | quirk | low (inferred; needs a login while a conversation is open) | XS | P3 | open; not pinned |
| RT-07: every timeline change runs about five passes over all loaded items: the `renderItems` rebuild and `reuseUnchangedRenderItems` (a map of every row), `findFirstUnreadKey`, `lastOwnMessageId`, `syncContentResizeObservations` (a `querySelectorAll` over every `li[data-event-id]`), and `countIncomingMessagesAfter` for a new message. Row reuse (`636ea5e9b`) keeps the DOM work to the changed rows; this script work stays linear in the loaded messages. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:281-341`, `:353`, `:380-393`, `:496-504`, `:511-533` | performance | low to medium (inferred, not measured; grows with long histories on weak devices) | M | P3 | open; not pinned |
| RT-08: the component reads `gameManager.chatConnection` and `gameManager.getCurrentGameScene()` when it is created, and `GameManager` reaches `UIWebsiteManager` through the `GameScene` import cycle. Every component test must mock both modules. | `RoomTimeline.svelte:81-82`, `:133-134` | design / import cycle (same family as MD-07) | low in production, high for tests | M (pass the connection and the room flags through the chat context) | P3 | open; worked around by two link seams |

## Smell Inventory rows

| Smell | Location | Refactoring | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Large component (1,096 lines, three parents: `RoomList.svelte`, `CompactConversation.svelte`, `ThreadPanel.svelte`) with four concerns: the header and its unread-elsewhere popover, the render items, the open and pagination sequence, and the scroll engine | `RoomTimeline.svelte` | Split along the pinch points: the header as its own component, the scroll engine (P3, P5, P6) as a plain module that takes the list element, the open sequence (P2) and the render items (P1) as functions of the room | open (Phase 2+) |
| Scroll state machine spread over flags and timers: `autoScroll`, `programmaticScrollKind`, `scrollAnchor`, `loadingMessagePromise`, five timers and three scroll kinds, written from eight handlers | `:102-131`, `:561-718` | Model it as one state machine (following, reading history, programmatic scroll, anchored, paginating) with explicit transitions; tests 5, 8 and 9 pin its effects | open |
